    "expanded": "Connecticut rose 17.2% to $68.7m. Pennsylvania's lead over the second-placed state widened to more than $25m. The report expects more $1bn months in the seasonally stronger closing months of 2026, putting the market on track for more than $12bn for the year. Expect operators to ask suppliers for better personalisation and more exclusive content to support growth in mature states.",
