    "summary": "Kalshi told the CFTC in a 28 September self-certification filing that it will end its Volume Incentive Program no earlier than 13 October. The programme had been due to run until 1 October 2027. It paid eligible traders a share of a fixed per-market reward in proportion to their volume, capped at $0.005 per contract. Kalshi gave no reason. In August, the CFTC issued an advisory on incentive programmes that warned of wash-trading risk.",
