    "summary": "ASOPOS, the Dominican association of point-of-sale software firms, has asked the government not to sign the new gambling law in its current wording. Its objection is to paragraphs 2 and 5 of Article 163, which could expose technology suppliers to criminal liability for what their clients do. The Senate passed the bill on 16 September and it was sent to President Abinader on 18 September. Its status is unclear because the 10-day constitutional deadline has passed with no publication. The law would replace rules dating from 1964 and bar new gaming venues for 10 years, except casinos in hotels and tourist zones.",
